From d171f09227f7dfe82002086729ea1d3b89052776 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:45:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 80/90] script: add the P2MR rescue lane to leaf version 0xe0

Once the tripwire disables elliptic curve checks in leaf version 0xe0,
a leaf such as <P> OP_CHECKSIG has no valid witness left. The rescue
lane (doc/p2mr-rescue.md, added later in this series) lets its owner
spend it by proving knowledge of the seed behind the key instead of
signing: in an executed leaf of version 0xe0, an OP_CHECKSIG,
OP_CHECKSIGVERIFY or OP_CHECKSIGADD with a 32-byte key whose signature
element is a rescue token, 0x03 || sid || pub, is checked with the proof
in the input's annex, 0x50 || 0x01 || proof. This happens before the
tripwire rule and whether elliptic curve checks are disabled or not, so
that the new SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_NO_RESCUE can be a restricting flag, as
every other flag is: with it, a token is a signature like any other. No
deployment lifts it yet.

The rules, in their order, after the 50 units every non-empty signature
pays and the key size:
- R1, a token only when its structure is that of SPEC.md section 7.5
  with a registered statement id (0x01), and never 64 or 65 bytes long,
  so that no element a node with the tripwire rules takes as a valid
  Schnorr signature is one;
- R2, VALIDATION_WEIGHT_PER_P2MR_RESCUE_CHECK, 100,000 and provisional
  until measured, before any hashing or parsing of the annex;
- R3, one rescue check per input, counted before the signature cache;
- R4, the annex is exactly one rescue record for the statement, which
  the P2MR branch now keeps as a span next to its hash;
- R5, 0 < y < n and x(y*G) equals the key, either parity, with
  libsecp256k1;
- R6, the rescue signature message, a SIGHASH_ALL-type message without
  sha_annex under the tag P2MR/Rescue/Sighash with key_version 3, the
  network id, the statement id and SHA256(pub), failing after
  MissingDataBehavior without the BIP 341 data;
- R7, voleith_verify_s1 over m = sighash || network id ||
  TaggedHash("P2MR/Rescue/Key", 0x00 || P), exactly 96 bytes;
- R8, a pass is a valid signature: OP_CHECKSIG pushes 1.

The network id comes with PrecomputedTransactionData; a transaction
without one fails R7. P2MRRescueProofVerifications counts the proofs
given to the library, for the tests of the signature cache. The caching checker keeps the result of R7 under
a fifth salted hasher, padded with 'R', keyed by m || sid || pub ||
proof. Four new script errors, P2MR_RESCUE_REPEAT, P2MR_RESCUE_ANNEX,
P2MR_RESCUE_KEY and P2MR_RESCUE_PROOF, also in the error names of
script_tests, and the flag name P2MR_NO_RESCUE, on bit 26; the
formatscriptflags test takes its unknown bits from far above it.
